Below is a complete CUDA C++ implementation of a min-heap with `push`, `pop`, and `heapify`, plus a set of unit tests covering edge cases. The heap is a single-threaded device-side structure that operates on an array in global or shared memory. For concurrent access, you would need to add locking (e.g., a mutex or atomic CAS loop).

