2. **Concurrent writes without synchronization.** `add()` performs a non-atomic read-modify-write on `bytearray` cells. If multiple threads add/check on the same instance concurrently, lost updates can leave some bits unset, causing false negatives for items that were actually added. Under high concurrent load, this breaks the usual Bloom filter guarantee of “no false negatives.”

