Two ways this can fail under load:

1. **Integer overflow in the prefix sum.**  
   Prefix sums grow with array length and value magnitude. Under large inputs, `long long` may overflow, causing undefined behavior for signed overflow and incorrect results.

2. **False sharing and barrier contention.**  
   The `block[tid]` entries are adjacent, so many threads writing them can hit the same cache line, causing heavy cache-line ping-ponging. Also, every block must reach the barriers, so under oversubscription or noisy-neighbor load, one delayed thread stalls all others and throughput collapses.

