// scan with strconv.ParseFloat. We allow digits, '.', and the 'e'/'E'
// exponent marker plus its sign. We deliberately do not try to fully
// validate here: strconv.ParseFloat does that and gives better errors.
func isNumberByte(b byte) bool {
	return (b >= '0' && b <= '9') || b == '.' || b == 'e' || b == 'E' || b == '+' || b == '-'
