Below is a complete CUDA C++ implementation of Kahn’s topological sort using a parallel frontier. It reports a cycle when the graph cannot be fully topologically sorted. The tests use a small assertion-style harness and cover empty graphs, self-loops, cycles, disconnected DAGs, duplicate edges, and larger DAGs.

```cpp
