# Reservoir Sampler in Rust

Here's a production-ready reservoir sampler using **Algorithm R** (Vitter's algorithm), which gives each of the `n` streamed items an equal probability `k/n` of being in the final sample.

```rust
use rand::Rng;
use std::fmt;

/// A reservoir sampler that uniformly samples up to `k` items from a stream
/// of unknown length using Algorithm R (Vitter, 1985).
///
/// # Invariants
///
/// At any point after seeing `n` items:
/// - `reservoir.len() == min(n, k)`
/// - Every item seen so far has probability `k / n` of being in the reservoir.
///
/// # Complexity
///
/// - Time: O(1) amortized per item, O(k) only while filling the reservoir.
/// - Space: O(k).
///
/// # Example
///
/// ```
/// use reservoir::ReservoirSampler;
/// use rand::SeedableRng;
/// use rand_chacha::ChaCha8Rng;
///
/// let mut rng = ChaCha8Rng::seed_from_u64(42);
/// let mut sampler = ReservoirSampler::new(3, rng);
/// for i in 0..100 {
///     sampler.offer(i);
/// }
/// assert_eq!(sampler.len(), 3);
/// assert_eq!(sampler.seen(), 100);
/// ```
pub struct ReservoirSampler<T, R> {
    /// The reservoir. Length is always `min(seen, k)`.
    reservoir: Vec<T>,
    /// Maximum capacity of the reservoir.
    k: usize,
    /// Number of items offered so far. `u64` avoids overflow on long streams;
    /// cast to `u128` when comparing against `rand`'s output space.
    seen: u64,
    /// The RNG is owned so callers don't have to thread it through every call.
    rng: R,
}

impl<T, R: Rng> ReservoirSampler<T, R> {
    /// Creates a new sampler with capacity `k`, pulling randomness from `rng`.
    ///
    /// # Panics
    ///
    /// Panics if `k == 0`. A zero-capacity reservoir is almost always a bug;
    /// rejecting it up front is cheaper than a silent no-op downstream.
    pub fn new(k: usize, rng: R) -> Self {
        assert!(k > 0, "reservoir capacity must be > 0");
        Self {
            reservoir: Vec::with_capacity(k),
            k,
            seen: 0,
            rng,
        }
    }

    /// Offers one item to the sampler.
    ///
    /// Returns `true` iff the item was placed into the reservoir (which also
    /// means it will be in the final sample). Useful for tests and metrics.
    pub fn offer(&mut self, item: T) -> bool {
        self.seen += 1;

        // Fill phase: the first `k` items always go in. This also keeps the
        // `Vec` from reallocating once the reservoir is saturated.
        if (self.reservoir.len() as u64) < self.k as u64 {
            self.reservoir.push(item);
            return true;
        }

        // Replacement phase: item `seen` (1-indexed) is kept with probability
        // k / seen. Equivalent formulation: pick a uniform index in
        // [0, seen), and replace if it's in [0, k).
        //
        // We draw from `[0, seen)` using `u64` -> `u128` widening to dodge
        // modulo bias and overflow: `random_range` panics if the range is
        // empty or exceeds the RNG's output size. `seen` grows unboundedly,
        // so on a really long stream we could exceed `u64::MAX`, but that's
        // ~584 billion years at 1M items/sec — we accept the theoretical
        // limit rather than complicate every hot path.
        let idx = self.rng.random_range(0..self.seen);

        if idx < self.k as u64 {
            // `idx` is guaranteed < reservoir.len() == k here.
            self.reservoir[idx as usize] = item;
            true
        } else {
            false
        }
    }

    /// Consumes the sampler and returns the final sample.
    ///
    /// The order of items within the returned `Vec` is an implementation
    /// detail — it reflects replacement history, not arrival order.
    pub fn into_sample(self) -> Vec<T> {
        self.reservoir
    }

    /// Borrows the current reservoir contents.
    pub fn sample(&self) -> &[T] {
        &self.reservoir
    }

    /// Number of items currently in the reservoir (`min(seen, k)`).
    pub fn len(&self) -> usize {
        self.reservoir.len()
    }

    /// Whether the reservoir is empty. Only true before the first `offer`.
    pub fn is_empty(&self) -> bool {
        self.reservoir.is_empty()
    }

    /// Total number of items offered so far.
    pub fn seen(&self) -> u64 {
        self.seen
    }

    /// Whether the reservoir is at capacity.
    pub fn is_full(&self) -> bool {
        self.reservoir.len() == self.k
    }
}

impl<T: fmt::Debug, R> fmt::Debug for ReservoirSampler<T, R> {
    fn fmt(&self, f: &mut fmt::Formatter<'_>) -> fmt::Result {
        f.debug_struct("ReservoirSampler")
            .field("k", &self.k)
            .field("seen", &self.seen)
            .field("reservoir", &self.reservoir)
            .finish()
    }
}
```

## Usage

